 "_comment": "Shared by the Go unit.dropin handler test and the Ruby System::UnitDropinService spec: one table, two implementations of the directive allow-list, the capability-subset rule and the renderer. A value that is a string is literal; an object expands to prefix + repeat*times + suffix (token-shaped values are built at run time, never written out). 'accepted' and 'refused' entries are whole directive lists; 'capability_subset' pairs a list with the unit's resolved capability set (null = unresolvable); 'render' pins the exact file both sides write.",
